Analyze the code base of the project related to the vulnerability.
Try to locate the entrypoint of the project that can reach the vulnerability.
Also figure out the data that is needed to trigger the vulnerability.
The entrypoint may be:
  a main() function if the code containing the vulnerability compiles to a command line program, or
  a web interface if the project (or one of its modules) compiles to a web server and the code containing the vulnerability is used by the some service in it, or
  an exposed function if the code containing the vulnerability compiles to a library which provides functionalities to the outer world.

** Output **
ENTRYPOINT_TYPE: MAIN_FUNCTION, WEB_INTERFACE or EXPOSED_FUNCTION.
ENTRYPOINT: the full class name of the MAIN_FUNCTION, the module and the path of the WEB_INTERFACE or the and full class name and function name of the exposed function.
DATA: the data that is needed to trigger the vulnerability.
